        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Buy the NordicTrack Commercial 1250 if you will run as well as walk
            and want a full-size folding deck with decline for the least money NordicTrack asks.</strong>
            The current model, NTL14125, has a 22 by 60-inch belt, a 400 lb rating, -3% to 12% incline,
            12 mph and a 10-inch tilting screen, and was selling for about $1,600 on 14 October 2026. Plan
            around the two-year motor warranty and the one-year screen and labour terms, and price in iFIT
            if you will use the screen.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you run hard and often or want lifetime motor cover, the
            <a href="/nordictrack-commercial-1750-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Commercial 1750</a>
            is the step up. Whichever you choose, buy by model number, not by name.
